v 3
d dashboardbuilder: build a self-contained interactive HTML dashboard from Stata
d
d A putdocx-style builder: init -> tab -> panel -> build. Each panel call
d snapshots the data currently in memory; build writes ONE self-contained
d HTML file (inline JSON data, readable vanilla SVG/JS charts, no CDN).
d Tabs; kpi/line/bar/hbar/compare/table panels plus an html panel that inlines
d an external HTML file (e.g. a sparkta2 map) as an iframe; a selector dropdown
d with a reference-unit overlay; per-panel CSV/PNG downloads; save-as-PDF;
d callout and source notes; Texas 2036 or neutral theming; and a build receipt
d listing what likely still needs a human pass.
d
d Requires: Stata 16+ and a Python 3 visible to Stata (standard library
d only; nothing to pip install). See help dashboardbuilder.
d
d Author: Eric Booth, Texas 2036 Data & Research
d License: MIT
d Distribution-Date: 20260714
d Version: 1.2.0
d
